 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2022-05-18",
   "text": "Price Relief, Innovation, and Competition for Essential Drugs Act or the PRICED Act\n This bill allows biosimilars to be marketed five years after the reference brand-name biological product is licensed. Currently, brand-name biological products are provided a 12-year marketing-exclusivity period.\n This shortened marketing-exclusivity period applies only to biological products licensed by the Food and Drug Administration after enactment of this bill."
  }
 ],
